  "domain": "machine-learning",
  "definition": "The minimisation of objective functions that are not convex, so the loss surface may contain multiple local minima, saddle points, plateaus, and ravines, and no general guarantee links a local solution to the global optimum. Non-convex optimisation is the actual setting of deep learning\u2014neural network training landscapes are highly non-convex\u2014and of many engineering problems, tackled in practice with stochastic gradient methods, momentum, restarts, relaxations, and problem-specific structure rather than the clean certificates available in the convex case.",
